L000915	\section{Numerical evidence for the assumption on the Gaussianity of fluctuations}
L000916	\label{app:CLT}
L000917	
L000918	Previous work \cite{YueG2024,IrvG2025} has shown numerically
L000919	that finite-size fluctuations in the Kuramoto-Sakaguchi model (\ref{Eq:KS:original})
L000920	constitute a Gaussian process, consistent with an underlying central limit theorem.
L000921	For completeness, we provide here further numerical evidence.
L000922	Fig.~\ref{Fig:Gaussianity}(a) and (b) show the empirical histogram
L000923	of the real and the imaginary part of the fluctuations $\zeta$
L000924	obtained from a long time simulation over $50,000$ time units
L000925	with a sampling time of $dt=0.05$ of the KS model together
L000926	with a best fit Gaussian clearly establishing the Gaussian character of the fluctuations.
L000927	For $K=3$ we find a value of the skewness for the real and imaginary part
L000928	of the fluctuations $\zeta$ of $-0.058$ and $-0.051$, respectively,
L000929	and a kurtosis of $2.98$ for both. We further show in Fig.~\ref{Fig:Gaussianity}(c)
L000930	the empirical histogram for the temporal derivative of the mean phase
L000931	of the entrained oscillators $\tfrac{d}{dt}{\rm{arg}} Z_c(t)$,
L000932	which also shows a clear Gaussian statistics,
L000933	consistent with the phase diffusion discussed below.
